# 29. Important Security Principle — Least Privilege

PSS aligns closely with the **principle of least privilege**.

The idea is:

> Give a workload only the privileges and access it actually requires.

Instead of:

```text
Pod
 │
 ├── privileged
 ├── root
 ├── hostNetwork
 ├── hostPID
 ├── all capabilities
 └── unrestricted access
```

we want:

```text
Pod
 │
 ├── non-root
 ├── no privilege escalation
 ├── minimal capabilities
 ├── seccomp
 └── restricted host access
```

This reduces the potential impact of a compromised container.

