# 30. Common PSS/PSA Problems

### Problem 1 — Pod runs as root

```text
runAsNonRoot requirement violated
```

Fix by configuring:

```yaml
runAsNonRoot: true
```

and ensuring the image supports non-root execution.

---

### Problem 2 — Privileged container

```yaml
privileged: true
```

Restricted policies reject this.

Remove it unless genuinely required.

---

### Problem 3 — Privilege escalation enabled

Fix:

```yaml
allowPrivilegeEscalation: false
```

---

### Problem 4 — Missing seccomp

Use:

```yaml
seccompProfile:
  type: RuntimeDefault
```

when required by the selected PSS level.

---

### Problem 5 — Existing workloads break after enforcement

Possible reason:

```text
Namespace
   │
   ▼
enforce=restricted
   │
   ▼
Existing workload violates Restricted
   │
   ▼
Pod creation/update rejected
```

Use `warn` and `audit` to identify violations before enforcement.

