# 🎯 Final Takeaway

The most important thing I learned about Pod Security Standards is:

> **PSS defines security requirements for Pods, while Pod Security Admission (PSA) can apply those requirements to namespaces using `enforce`, `audit`, and `warn` modes.**

The three profiles are:

```text
Privileged
    ↓
Minimal restrictions

Baseline
    ↓
Blocks common privilege-escalation risks

Restricted
    ↓
Strong workload hardening
```

And the overall Kubernetes security model can be thought of as:

```text
                Kubernetes Security
                       │
       ┌───────────────┼────────────────┐
       │               │                │
      RBAC       NetworkPolicy       PSS/PSA
       │               │                │
   API access      Network access   Pod security
       │               │                │
       └───────────────┼────────────────┘
                       │
                       ▼
              Defense in Depth
```

PSS is an important Kubernetes security concept because it helps organizations enforce safer workload configurations and reduce the privileges available to potentially compromised containers.

